message: "If you use this project, please cite it as below."
title: "German Academic AI-Text Detector: Human-Written, AI-Generated and AI-Assisted German Academic Text"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Issa
    given-names: Ali
  - family-names: Hijazi
    given-names: Hassan
repository-code: "https://github.com/aliissa824/German-AI-Text-Detector-from-scratch"
url: "https://huggingface.co/aliissa824"
license: MIT
date-released: 2026-10-14
keywords:
  - AI text detection
  - AI-assisted writing
  - German
  - academic writing
  - natural language processing
  - text classification
  - transformers
abstract: >-
  A three-class detector that classifies German academic text as
  human-written, AI-generated, or AI-assisted (human text rewritten and
  polished by a language model). The project builds a dataset of 30,629
  texts from openly licensed German academic papers and four AI models,
  and compares a zero-shot LLM, a TF-IDF baseline and five fine-tuned
  transformer models, including significance tests, learning curves and
  an analysis of which texts are hardest to detect.
